        <item>
            <title>0.4.0</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 07 Aug 2026 13:50:20 +0800</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>9</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.4.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[- A wrong turn can now be taken back. Whenever there's a step behind you, a small chevron appears
  at the top left of the overlay — or press ⌘[. Going back animates the way it came.
- Answering "Yes, I'm done" is no longer irreversible: go back from the congratulations page and
  your session is still running, exactly as you left it. The same goes for finishing on a return.
- What you typed as your intention now survives going back to the naming screen and returning to it.
]]></description>
